<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sack of Rome (410)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/410">410 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 410 CE was the capture and plunder of the city by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> under Alaric. It was the first time in about eight centuries that Rome had fallen to a foreign enemy, and it caused deep shock across the Roman world. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> treat it as a symbol of the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a>, which ended in 476 CE.</p></div>
